# Task Routing

The eight `rd-*` skills can be used independently and in any order. They are not a forced pipeline.

## Available Skills

| Skill | Deliverable | Daily work |
|---|---|---|
| `$rd-requirements-analysis` | Structured requirements document or PRD | Requirements analysis |
| `$rd-technical-writing` | Technical proposal, high-level design, or implementation plan | Solution design |
| `$rd-detailed-design` | Detailed design document | API, data, flow, and failure design |
| `$rd-implement` | Runnable code and tests | Implementation and bug fixing |
| `$rd-doc-review` | Document review findings | Requirements, proposal, or design review |
| `$rd-code-review` | Code review findings | Diff, PR, commit, or working tree review |
| `$rd-testing` | Test plan, tests, or test report | Test design and execution |
| `$rd-deployment` | Runbook or release checklist | Deployment and rollback planning |

## Authoring To Review Mapping

| Authoring skill | Review skill | Review mode |
|---|---|---|
| `$rd-requirements-analysis` to PRD | `$rd-doc-review` | Requirements Review |
| `$rd-technical-writing` to proposal or implementation plan | `$rd-doc-review` | Proposal Review |
| `$rd-detailed-design` to detailed design | `$rd-doc-review` | Design Review |
| `$rd-implement` to code | `$rd-code-review` | Code Review |

## Invocation Guidance

- Invoke the relevant skill by name when the task clearly matches it.
- Do not force a full requirements-to-deployment pipeline for small tasks.
- For reviews, lead with findings and severity.
- For implementation, make the smallest verifiable change and run the closest checks.
- For testing, cover normal, abnormal, and boundary scenarios.

## Parallel Work

Use parallel or background work only when subtasks are independent, write scopes do not overlap, and the outputs can be merged without ambiguity.
